rolo-brain (Project Rolo)
================================================================

This work distributes a fine-tuned model derived from Google's 
Gemma 3 4B Instruction-Tuned model for [Project Rolo](https://github.com/larawashington/Desktop-Pet).
The fine-tune is published as a LoRA delta fused into the base 
weights and quantized to GGUF (Q5_K_M) for distribution via 
Ollama.

----------------------------------------------------------------
Base model
----------------------------------------------------------------

Component:  google/gemma-3-4b-it (Gemma 3 4B Instruction-Tuned)
Owner:      Google
License:    Gemma Terms of Use
Link:       https://ai.google.dev/gemma/terms

Use of this model is subject to the Gemma Terms of Use including
the Gemma Prohibited Use Policy
(https://ai.google.dev/gemma/prohibited_use_policy). Downstream 
users of `rolo-brain` are bound by those terms as if they had 
downloaded the base Gemma 3 model directly.

The base weights used for fine-tuning were taken from the MLX
community 4-bit conversion:

  mlx-community/gemma-3-4b-it-4bit
  https://huggingface.co/mlx-community/gemma-3-4b-it-4bit

----------------------------------------------------------------
Fine-tune (LoRA delta)
----------------------------------------------------------------

Component:  rolo-brain adapter (LoRA delta)
Author:     Lara Washington
License:    Apache License 2.0 (delta only; base model retains
            its own Gemma Terms of Use)

Training method:    LoRA (r=16, scale=2.0), completion-only loss
Trainer:            mlx-lm 0.31.3
Seed:               20260515
Training corpus:    ~3,400 SFT rows, supervised dialogue/speech
                    matched to a Rust runtime's first-user-turn
                    contract (see `runtime_contract.md`).

----------------------------------------------------------------
Training-data provenance
----------------------------------------------------------------

The supervised fine-tuning corpus was assembled from:

  1. A hand-written gold-seed set authored by Lara Washington.
  2. A synthetic dialogue corpus distilled from DeepSeek V4-Pro
     (DeepSeek-AI, MIT-licensed weights with distillation
     explicitly permitted by the publisher's terms).
  3. A small mix of databricks-dolly-15k (CC BY-SA 3.0) rows to
     preserve general instruction-following.
  4. Quality-filtered by Kimi K2.6 (Moonshot AI, modified MIT)
     acting as a judge model.
  5. A small "defense seed" of hand-written boundary-teaching
     rows authored by Lara Washington.

All training-data sources permit derivative fine-tunes.

----------------------------------------------------------------
Inference contract
----------------------------------------------------------------

The model expects a specific first-user-turn layout (state header
+ blank line + user/<idle> body); see the `runtime_contract.md`
included in this repository. Sending a `system` role to this
model is OFF-DISTRIBUTION and will degrade output quality —
persona is in the weights, not in a system prompt.

